    {
      "id": "claim_585989e22b60432e80fcc7a6e26ef1be",
      "statement": "The installed package has a lightweight core dependency set (`html2text`, `primp`, and `selectolax`) and registers the `quack` console command at `quack.cli:main`; JavaScript rendering is isolated in the optional `render` extra, which depends on SeleniumBase.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://pyproject.toml#L1-L31",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f71739b78e82c1d17cbb2dc45dd24a8acf66d06991c86eaef4a5d925209a384e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2c465e8ada594267b33e758ca328a4fa",
      "statement": "`quack` is the package façade: it re-exports search/fetch, `main`, the library error types, and query/result helpers through `__all__`; `render` and `RenderError` are added to that export list only when importing `.render` succeeds.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://quack/__init__.py#L3-L44",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4f8b4a9c216cd8bffc733319f48c9e45c5138b41ec2761e34578e756022e5cc8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_357a4aa5d54f4737bfc64e0f387d887a",
      "statement": "Render export/import success does not prove SeleniumBase is installed: `render()` imports SeleniumBase lazily and raises `RenderError` with installation guidance if that import fails, while the CLI independently performs its own guarded render import and availability check before dispatching the render command.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://quack/cli.py#L125-L144",
